-- title:
--   Completed local ring at a singular point of the X₁(Mp) model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 5$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`. Write $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlgFin` of $K$ generated by $j$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` generated by $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ and $\varpi_z \in \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase`; assume $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak{m}_z$ and that $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}/(\varpi_z)$ is not a regular local ring. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ (complete for the $\mathfrak{m}_W$-adic topology) and a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, together with a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}_z$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel W (σ ϖ)`](def/ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel.html#L15) $= W[[U,V]]/(UV - \sigma\varpi)$ (the quotient of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\sigma\varpi)$), such that for every $a \in A$ the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ is carried by $e$ to the class of the constant series $\sigma a$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem at the non-regular (supersingular crossing) points of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$: the completed local ring is an ordinary crossing $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi)$ with $\varpi$ still a uniformiser of $W$, so that the crossing exponent is one. It is used to derive the statement that $\varpi_z$ factors as $uv$ with $\mathfrak{m}_z = (u,v)$, the input for the regularity and semistability properties of the model.
